  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2509.10054v1</id>
    <title>XAgents: A Unified Framework for Multi-Agent Cooperation via IF-THEN Rules and Multipolar Task Processing Graph</title>
    <updated>2025-09-12T08:40:58Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.10054v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.10054v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>The rapid advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs) has significantly enhanced the capabilities of Multi-Agent Systems (MAS) in supporting humans with complex, real-world tasks. However, MAS still face challenges in effective task planning when handling highly complex tasks with uncertainty, often resulting in misleading or incorrect outputs that hinder task execution. To address this, we propose XAgents, a unified multi-agent cooperative framework built on a multipolar task processing graph and IF-THEN rules. XAgents uses the multipolar task processing graph to enable dynamic task planning and handle task uncertainty. During subtask processing, it integrates domain-specific IF-THEN rules to constrain agent behaviors, while global rules enhance inter-agent collaboration. We evaluate the performance of XAgents across three distinct datasets, demonstrating that it consistently surpasses state-of-the-art single-agent and multi-agent approaches in both knowledge-typed and logic-typed question-answering tasks. The codes for XAgents are available at: https://github.com/AGI-FHBC/XAgents.</summary>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2025-09-12T08:40:58Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.AI"/>
    <author>
      <name>Hailong Yang</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Mingxian Gu</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Jianqi Wang</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Guanjin Wang</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Zhaohong Deng</name>
    </author>
